    "method": "Sentinel-2 composite renders at 3 km, 1.5 km and 700 m (RGB, NIR, brightness, edge). The archaeological area is the tree-covered, brown and bare textured ground of about 1 km by 1 km immediately south-west of the dense modern town of Harappa, matching Vats 1940 Plate I, where the mounds F, AB and E lie west and south-west of the town and south of the old bed of the Ravi. The point is the middle of that textured area; individual mounds could not be delimited with confidence at 10 m."
